{"id":"6f8348d1-fe02-486e-8758-dc545470e4ca","object":"chat.completion","created":1784826040,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    nodes = payload['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(payload['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    # build children\\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            children[p].append(n['id'])\\n    # identify mandatory nodes (non-removable)\\n    mandatory = set(n['id'] for n in nodes if not n['removable'])\\n    kept = set(mandatory)\\n    # for each required symbol, ensure at least one node with that symbol is kept\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if any(node_map[nid]['symbol'] == sym for nid in kept):\\n            continue\\n        # find all removable nodes with this symbol\\n        candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['symbol'] == sym and n['removable']]\\n        if not candidates:\\n            # symbol not present or only non-removable but not in kept? already handled\\n            continue\\n        best = None\\n        best_score = -1\\n        best_added = None\\n        for cand in candidates:\\n            # compute path from cand to root\\n            added_nodes = set()\\n            cur = cand['id']\\n            while cur is not None and cur not in kept:\\n                added_nodes.add(cur)\\n                cur = node_map[cur]['parent']\\n            # also need to include ancestors that are not yet kept; those are already in added_nodes\\n            # score = sum of utility of added nodes\\n            score = sum(node_map[nid]['utility'] for nid in added_nodes)\\n            if score > best_score:\\n                best_score = score\\n                best = cand['id']\\n                best_added = added_nodes\\n        if best is not None:\\n            kept.update(best_added)\\n    # return list of kept node ids\\n    return {'kept_ids': sorted(kept)}\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to output a JSON object with a single key \"implementation\" whose value is a Python source string defining `solve(case)`. The problem: \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\". The input case has nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. Also required_symbols. The goal: reduce the tree by deleting removable nodes and possibly replacing? But the description says \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an interestingness oracle\". The provided fixtures show only input shapes. We need to infer the task.\n\nGiven the name \"SE-PE-01\" and \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\", likely the task is to remove removable nodes such that the resulting tree still satisfies required symbols at each depth? Or preserve \"interestingness\" which might be some utility threshold? But no oracle is provided in the input. Perhaps the oracle is that the tree must contain all required_symbols? And we want to minimize total utility? Or maximize? The nodes have utility values. The goal might be to reduce the tree by removing removable nodes, but we cannot remove non-removable nodes. And we need to ensure that for each required symbol, there is at least one node with that symbol in the tree? Also the tree structure must be valid: each node's parent must exist, depth must be consistent.\n\nBut the problem says \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates\". Possibly we need to consider that nodes can be replaced by their children? Or we can remove a node and promote its children? That would be \"replacement\". However, the fixtures don't give any grammar rules. There is \"symbol\" field which might be a grammar symbol. The required_symbols list are symbols that must be present. The task might be to prune the tree by deleting removable nodes, but we cannot delete a node if it would remove a requ